course: dictionary
lesson: 823
title: Belladonna, a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Belladonna can name a plant, and it can also name a drug made from that plant. «Deadly nightshade has tempting shiny black berries» is about the plant, because berries grow on plants.
explain: Look for clue words. Words like poison and deadly show that the plant is harmful. The sentence «Its other name, belladonna, means beautiful lady» tells you that belladonna is also a name, and that the name can hide a danger.
explain: The word comes from Italian, and «beautiful lady» is what it means. Long ago some women put drops of it in their eyes to make their pupils look bigger. It was dangerous, so a pretty name can hide a poison, and that is a good reason to check before you trust a word or a berry.
fact: Belladonna is a noun. It is a very poisonous plant, also called deadly nightshade.
fact: The plant has purple flowers and shiny black berries.
fact: A drug made from belladonna is used carefully in medicine, for example to widen the pupils of the eyes.
fact: Belladonna means «beautiful lady» in Italian.
fact: Never eat berries you do not know, even if they look shiny and tempting.
exercise: «Deadly nightshade has tempting shiny black berries.» Why might the berries be dangerous to eat? | They smell of smoke | They are green and sour | *They look tempting, but they are poisonous | They are heavy and hard to pick
exercise: In «belladonna, means beautiful lady in Italian», which language is the name from? | Spanish | Scots | French | *Italian
exercise: Why should you never eat berries you do not know? | *Some wild berries are poisonous, like those of belladonna | They make your eyes bigger | They are sweet and taste of sugar | They are only for birds
test: Belladonna can mean a plant or a drug. In «a drug made from this plant, used carefully in medicine», which meaning is used? | The plant with purple flowers | *The drug made from the plant | A shiny black berry | A poisonous insect
test: Why did some women put drops of belladonna in their eyes long ago? | To cure their colds | To keep the sun out of their eyes | *To make their pupils big, so their eyes looked bigger
exam: What is the safest thing to do if you find shiny black berries you do not know? | Taste one to check | Eat a few, they look tasty | Put them in your pocket to share | *Leave them alone and tell an adult
